From 8bf8b9fb1df696ebfd93c4d8677bbc56fb14d362 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mesa-nvk-horizon <mesa-nvk-horizon@localhost>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 07:11:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 68/68] vulkan/wsi: Horizon, the acquire meter counts the
 deferral, not the GPU
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

mesa-nvk-horizon: Phase 6 item 4 (Horizon WSI backend)
Why: the counter 0066 added said "handed that fence to the GPU instead
 of waiting for it". It is incremented in the acquire, at the moment the
 WSI decides not to wait — which is before anything is known about how
 the dependency will be consumed.
 .
 What consumes it is whatever the application does with the semaphore
 and the fence it was just given. An application that takes the fence
 and calls vkWaitForFences on it has waited on the CPU, and this counter
 reads exactly the same as for one that put the semaphore in a submit's
 wait list. That is not a corner case: it is what t_vk_present_draw,
 t_vk_swapchain and t_vk_wsi_mt all do, so the first console run would
 have produced a full count of "handed to the GPU" on three tests where
 no GPU wait was emitted at all. Raised in review of the branch.
 .
 So the line says what it measures — the fence was left for the acquire
 semaphore or fence to carry — and names the counter that says the other
 thing: nvkmd_horizon's "wait(s) handed to the host engine", which 0049
 increments after horizon_gpu_submit_waits() has taken the batch. The
 two read together are the claim; either alone is not.
 .
 Only the wording and the comment change; the arithmetic is the same
 counter in the same place, because the place is right for what it now
 says it counts.
Evidence: CROSS BUILD, scripts/ci-build-archives.sh over
 ghcr.io/d3fau4/nx-dev:latest (aarch64-none-elf-gcc 15.2.0, meson
 1.11.2, -Wall -Wextra -Werror): wsi_horizon.c compiles with no warning
 and libvulkan_wsi.a links. The line itself has never been printed by a
 console. NO CONSOLE HAS RUN THIS.
Upstream: no — it is a Horizon-only backend's own instrumentation.
---
 src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c
index c46fbc6..c49b351 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c
@@ -752,12 +752,31 @@ struct wsi_horizon_acquire_meter {
 
    uint32_t acquires;
    uint32_t rounds;          /* dequeues that answered "come back later" */
-   /* Of the acquires, the ones that handed the release fence on instead
-    * of waiting for it. Counted separately and not folded into a mean,
-    * because the two are not the same measurement: a deferred acquire's
-    * total says nothing about when the buffer became usable, only about
-    * when its index did. A window with a mix in it would report a mean
-    * that is neither. */
+   /* Of the acquires, the ones that left the release fence for somebody
+    * else to wait on.
+    *
+    * IT COUNTS THE DEFERRAL AND NOT THE GPU, and the difference is the
+    * whole reason it is named this way. It is incremented here, where
+    * the WSI decides not to wait — before anything is known about how
+    * the dependency will be consumed. Whether it becomes a host-engine
+    * SYNCPOINT acquire depends on what the application does with the
+    * semaphore and fence it was given afterwards, and an application
+    * that takes the fence and calls vkWaitForFences on it has waited on
+    * the CPU with this counter reading the same as an application that
+    * did not. An earlier wording said "handed that fence to the GPU",
+    * which claimed the second thing while measuring the first.
+    *
+    * The counter that says the GPU did the waiting is nvkmd_horizon's,
+    * "wait(s) handed to the host engine"
+    * (MESA_VK_NVKMD_HORIZON_SUBMIT_STATS=1): it is incremented after
+    * horizon_gpu_submit_waits() has actually taken the batch. Read the
+    * two together — this one says the acquire stopped waiting, that one
+    * says the GPU started.
+    *
+    * Counted separately and not folded into a mean, because a deferred
+    * acquire's total says nothing about when the buffer became usable,
+    * only about when its index did. A window with a mix in it would
+    * report a mean that is neither. */
    uint32_t deferred;
    uint64_t total_ns;
    uint64_t fence_ns;        /* of the total, inside nvMultiFenceWait  */
@@ -1527,8 +1546,9 @@ wsi_horizon_meter_acquire(struct wsi_horizon_swapchain *chain,
              " acquire(s), mean %" PRIu64 " us (max %" PRIu64 "), of which "
              "%" PRIu64 " us waiting for a free buffer over %" PRIu32
              " dequeue round(s) and %" PRIu64 " us on the compositor's "
-             "release fence; %" PRIu32 " handed that fence to the GPU "
-             "instead of waiting for it",
+             "release fence; %" PRIu32 " left that fence for the acquire "
+             "semaphore or fence to carry (whether the GPU then waited on "
+             "it is nvkmd_horizon's counter, not this one)",
              (now_ns - m->window_start_ns) / 1000000u, m->acquires,
              m->total_ns / m->acquires / 1000u, m->max_total_ns / 1000u,
              (m->total_ns - m->fence_ns) / m->acquires / 1000u, m->rounds,
